.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBrift\fR compares two large text files under a heap limit set
with \fB\-\-mem\fR. It writes a unified diff that \fBpatch\fR(1)
applies to \fIA\fR to get \fIB\fR. Its other modes print a summary, open
a terminal view, or compare records by key.
.PP
Rift hashes every line once and cuts the pair into segments at lines that
occur once in each file. Segments with identical bytes are equal. The
others are refined on demand.
.PP
In the \fB\-\-\-\fR and \fB+++\fR lines a file name is quoted as GNU diff
3.10 on x86_64 quotes it: a name with a space, a control character,
\fB"\fR, \fB\e\fR or a byte above 0x7f is wrapped in double quotes, with
C escapes and octal bytes (\fB"caf\e303\e251"\fR). Other names are printed
as given. On aarch64 that diff prints bytes above 0x7f raw; Rift does not.
.PP
Rift does not look for binary files. A NUL byte is part of a line, and the
diff prints it in the \fB\-\fR and \fB+\fR lines. There is no
"Binary files differ" message. \fBpatch\fR still applies the output.
